  "summary": "Remote-controlled coding agent: Telegram/web messages drive shell execution on installer's host",
  "details": "@inetafrica/open-claudia is an always-on bot that connects out to Telegram (api.telegram.org long-poll), a Kazee channel, and a local web/voice dashboard, and routes inbound messages from remote chats through core/router.js → runAgent() in core/runner.js. runAgent spawns Claude Code / OpenAI Codex CLI subprocesses (via child_process spawn/execFileSync) in the installer's workspace with full shell and file-edit tool access, gated only by an in-chat owner-approval prompt in core/tool-guard.js. Any chatId the owner approves (core/access.js isChatAuthorized) can then send messages that cause arbitrary commands to execute on the host running the bot. Additional files (setup.js, health.js, bot.js) contact api.telegram.org and huggingface.co and read process.env/process.platform for bot bootstrap and health reporting. The network-source → local shell/exec dataflow is a remote-controlled backdoor into the host running the package, whether framed as a coding-assistant bot or not.",
